# Expected-failure (xfail) cases from tests/ok.lst.
# These exercise known-broken engine behavior in tiny-regex-c:
#   - {n,} quantifiers report match length 2 regardless of the actual run
#   - group (...) + quantifier (+/{n}) does not match
# See README.md ("Broke recursive pattern matching") and the TODO notes.
# A natural failure here is tolerated; an unexpected pass (XPASS) fails CI.
\w{2,}			"abc"		3
[a-z]{2,}		"abcd"		4
([a-z][0-9])+		"a0b1"		4
([a-z][0-9]){3}		"a0b1c2"	6